NEXI TTS is a local driver for upstream KittenML Kitten TTS Nano 0.8 int8 and Mini 0.8.
It is NOT a NEXI-trained or fine-tuned model.

The character symbol table, phoneme tokenization, ONNX input construction,
voice style selection, speed priors, and trailing-sample trim derive from:
https://github.com/KittenML/KittenTTS/blob/0c61f684b54fe962e4b7c2fa0285ed75f64ad402/kittentts/onnx_model.py
KittenML/KittenTTS is released under Apache-2.0; see LICENSE.
Changes: offline verified asset loading, bounded punctuation-preserving chunks,
bounded English currency/unit/number normalization, explicit CPU threads and memory
options, validation, atomic streamed WAV writes, local WAV/PCM streaming API,
profile-specific immutable manifests, tests and measurement tools.

The upstream model cards declare Apache-2.0 for the nano-int8 and Mini weights.
The dependencies retain their own licenses, notably phonemizer and bundled
eSpeak NG under GPL-3.0. Distributing a complete application requires reviewing
those obligations separately from the Apache-2.0 model license.
